          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1\tWhen vision-language models are fine-tuned for robotic action prediction, which representational changes are associated with training and which are inherited from the pretrained backbone?\n2\tWe compare trained and reference checkpoints of three Vision-Language-Action models across four LIBERO task suites via layer-wise probes, attention profiling, and counterfactual perturbations.\n3\tWe find that VLM-to-VLA fine-tuning is associated with a consistent exit-layer collapse in action-probe decodability ($\\Delta R^2 = 0.16$--$0.46$) that is absent in VLA-to-VLA transitions ($\\Delta R^2 < 0.10$) and in three NLP instruction-tuning controls ($\\Delta R^2 = 0.000$), suggesting this reorganization is specific to action-oriented training rather than a generic fine-tuning artifact.\n4\tComplementary analyses reveal that trained VLAs develop substantial sensitivity to instruction content while the dominant attention patterns at early layers largely pre-exist in pretrained backbones.\n5\tThese findings provide a cross-architecture decomposition of instruction routing in fine-tuned VLAs, disentangling training-associated representational changes from inherited structure.\n6\t"
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "feishu:group:oc_a1d032cbe70bdd2058438e67e0d57613:director",
            "tool": "Read",
            "elapsed_ms": 571
          },
          "id": "event-000942"
        },
        {
          "source_line": 943,
          "timestamp": "2026-05-28T11:04:03.956782+00:00",
          "recorded_role": "tool",
          "role": "tool_call",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "called Read"
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "feishu:group:oc_a1d032cbe70bdd2058438e67e0d57613:director",
            "tool": "Read",
            "tool_args": {
              "file_path": "/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/docs/paper/discussion.tex"
            }
