          "id": "event-000943"
        },
        {
          "source_line": 944,
          "timestamp": "2026-05-28T11:04:04.007523+00:00",
          "recorded_role": "tool_result",
          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1\t\\section{Discussion and Conclusion}\n2\t\\label{sec:discussion}\n3\t\n4\t\\paragraph{Scope and limitations.}\\looseness=-1\n5\tAll findings are correlational (confounded by data distribution and optimization; $N = 2$ VLM-to-VLA transitions; Appendix~\\ref{sec:claim_evidence_appendix}); we analyze causal-decoder VLAs on LIBERO only (flow-matching~\\cite{black2024_pi0} and diffusion~\\cite{ghosh2024_octo} architectures may differ); all analyses are open-loop.\n6\tTrained $\\Delta R^2$ correlates with published success rates ($\\rho = 0.583$, $p = 0.10$; Appendix~\\ref{sec:extended_discussion_appendix}) but is underpowered ($n = 9$; effect size is large, $|\\rho| > 0.5$); tracing collapse onset remains for future work.\n7\t\n8\t\\paragraph{Practical implications and conclusion.}\\looseness=-1\n9\t$\\Delta R^2 > 0.10$ provides a cheap probe-based screening signal that can supplement rollout evaluation.\n10\tThe flat VLA-to-VLA $\\Delta R^2$ profile justifies staged pipelines that preserve exit structure, and mid-layer features (peak at L9--L11) outperform exit-layer representations where collapse is pronounced.\n11\tThe distributed instruction integration pattern (\\S\\ref{sec:routing_synthesis}) implies that uniform pruning may be preferable to attention-score-based head selection for VLA compression.\n12\tThe consistent three-way pattern provides a first cross-architecture decomposition of VLA instruction routing; extended implications are discussed in Appendix~\\ref{sec:extended_practical_implications}.\n13\tCode and data will be released upon acceptance.\n14\t"
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "feishu:group:oc_a1d032cbe70bdd2058438e67e0d57613:director",
            "tool": "Read",
            "elapsed_ms": 50
